The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
skb = skb_realloc_headroom(skb, MLXSW_TXHDR_LEN);
if (!skb) {
    dev_kfree_skb_any(skb_orig);
    return NETDEV_TX_OK;
}
```
Reason:
The code incorrectly assumes that the original socket buffer (`skb_orig`) will be automatically released during the reallocation process. However, `skb_realloc_headroom()` creates a new skb and does not free the original skb, leading to a memory leak when the reallocation is successful.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
dev_consume_skb_any(skb_orig);
```
Reason:
This statement ensures that the original skb (`skb_orig`) is properly released after the reallocation is successful, preventing the memory leak by explicitly consuming the original skb when it is no longer needed.

